<title>MEXICO: Mexico supermarket, department sales fall in July.</title>
<headline>Mexico supermarket, department sales fall in July.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales at Mexican department stores fell 3.8 percent in July compared to the same month the previous year, the National Association of Supermarket and Department Stores (ANTAD) said on Tuesday in a statement.</p>
<p>The decline came following two months of gains in department store sales.</p>
<p>Sales at supermarkets were down 8.0 percent compared to July of last year.</p>
<p>The figures were based on a national index of sales adjusted to a same-store basis, ANTAD said.</p>
<p>-- David Luhnow, Mexico City newsroom 525 7289565</p>
